+### MLP Opacity Regression
 Fusion ablation technique where opacity is regressed from an MLP using 8-dim feature vectors from HexPlane. Sets itself apart by boosting PSNR, SSIM, LPIPS at the cost of slower rendering. Choose when accuracy is prioritized over speed.
 
-### [MLPRender_Fea_WeakView](10541-mlprender-fea-weakview.md)
+### Gated Convolutions
 Output feature computed as $F_{output} = F_{input} + \phi(W_f \cdot F_{input}) \odot \sigma(W_g \cdot F_{input})$. Sets itself apart by dynamically selecting features for each channel and spatial location. Choose for filtering invalid features in driving scenes.
 
+### Convolutional Shading Network
+Learnable CNN applied to screen-space feature buffers to generate view-dependent RGB colors from neural radiance field features attached to mesh vertices. Sets itself apart by operating in screen space for real-time view synthesis. Choose for real-time neural rendering on meshes.
+
+### Color Prediction
+Predicts RGB color $\hat{c}$ for a 3D point $x$ and viewing direction $v$ using a second function $c_\theta$. Sets itself apart by computing analytical SDF gradients for normals and using a two-layer MLP. Choose for monocular geometric cue integration.
+
+### Color Feature Skip-Connection
+Parameter-free, lightweight skip-connection layer that mitigates diminished color vibrancy after passing through the MLP by blending the MLP prediction with the first four channels of the color feature interpreted as RGBA. Sets itself apart by being parameter-free and directly restoring color vibrancy. Choose for color feature preservation.
+
+### Vision-language Decoder MLP
+Five-layer MLP used to decode features into vision-language outputs. Sets itself apart by bridging 3D scene grids with language models. Choose for joint geometric and semantic scene understanding.
+
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of MLP layers and input dimension. The MLP is shallow (3 layers), making it fast per sample [S3, S8, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Proportional to the number of parameters in the MLP ($O(featureC \cdot in\_mlpC)$) [S3, S8, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Linear with respect to the number of MLP layers and input dimension [G]. The MLP is shallow (3 layers), making it fast per sample [S3, S8, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Proportional to the number of parameters in the MLP ($O(featureC \cdot in\_mlpC)$) [G].
